<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates higher on expected tightness.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates higher on expected tightness.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR)  were higher on Friday on an expected tightness in the market caused  by the additional reserve requirement, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks are viewing a tightening of liquidity. The new reserve requirement  will take out 21 billion pesos from the system,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>The central bank raised on Wednesday the liquidity reserve of banks  to four percent from three percent to mop up money that would have  shifted to peso speculation.</p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  AUG 1		 JULY 31</p>
<p>    1 W		24  1/16		22 1/4</p>
<p>    2 W		24			22 3/16</p>
<p>    1 M		23			21 3/8</p>
<p>    2 M		21 13/16		20 7/16</p>
<p>    3 M		20 11/16		19 9/16</p>
<p>    6 M		18  5/8		 18 1/16</p>
<p>    12M		17  1/8		 16 15/16</p>
<p>    VAL		4-Aug		   1-Aug</p>
<p>-- Lilian Karunungan (63 2) 841-8937</p>
